elayed us debut fills  a frustrating gap for american ghibli  fans while offering further proof of the  studio's incredibly consistent  commitment to quality  city people see forests and woods and  streams and they're happy because they  think what they're seeing is nature  apart from back deep in the mountains  almost everything you see here is the  work of a farmer  that's so  sure of course it is  the river the dam  and those woods planted  and the stream doug  irrigation  it's not just the paddies and the fields  everything has been touched by man  our ancestors cleared this and  cultivated that  encouraged mushrooms berries wild garlic  really yeah  the sceneries come about by lucky  accident  as people have struggled with nature to  get what they needed to survive  so without people  this scenery wouldn't have been here  no it wouldn't have  to get what they need from nature  farmers have to do a lot of different  things to make sure that nature will  continue to provide forever  [Music]  number four still walking  12 years after their beloved eldest son  june pay drowned while saving a  stranger's life kyohei and toshiko  welcomed their surviving children home  for a family reunion younger son ryota  still feels that his parents resent that  he isn't the one who died his new wife  yukari is awkwardly meeting the rest of  the family for the first time daughter  chinami streams to fill the  uncomfortable pauses with forced cheer  starring hiroshi ebay you yoshio harada  and directed by hirokazu karida critics  say hirokazu karita's film may seem  modest at first but this family drama  casts a delicate entrancing spell  oh  my  number three drive my car  two years after his wife's unexpected  death yusuke kafuku a renowned staged  actor and director receives an offer to  direct a production of uncle vanya at a  theater festival in hiroshima there he  meets masaki watari a taciturn young  woman assigned by the festival to  chauffeur him in his beloved red saab  9